{
 "about": "When the towers rose: for each area, today’s count of buildings of ten storeys or 30 m and over and the share of them standing by each year; for each island the share alone, for its towers outside the areas. The settlements let a year hold that share of the lots the zoning, the density and the value would raise a tower on, and never more than the count (DATA.md “Towers, dated”).",
